REASON: The uniform ordinary-curve pullback claim omits the actual rotating rational action. Its Borel bundle has z(z-kT)=0 and U3=rho3(Az), k=b*kappa,A=a(nu-k). For present rows with k nonzero, an integral class dz+lT squares to (d^2 k+2dl)zT+l^2 T^2, forcing d=l=0 for a square-zero class. Thus no map to the ordinary curve can yield the required unit fibre degree. At k0 the ordinary projection is valid. The actual map still gives the full third-power zero because9 divides k^2; no three-primary theorem refutation is inferred.
