REASON: The physical Tate weight w is correct, but D.MT3 uses it after normalizing only the other fixed component. The simultaneous subgroup automorphism z->z^(nu^{-1}), inverse z->z^nu, changes the elliptic weight to w/nu. With alpha_C=(a*nu)^{-1}alpha_p and g_C=(a*nu)s, the coefficient is P_C=(w^2/nu^2-1)/2 and P_p=(a*nu)P_C=(b/p-a*nu)/2. These explicit inverse maps repair the three a1,nu2 five-primary assignments and preserve D.MT3/tag020L.
